tation that creates one new archive — which trips `len(freshlyPackedRefs) > 0` and walks every *other* archive for repair, even though those other archives were already correct from a prior run. Two reasonable fixes:\n   - **Version-tag** `generation.json` (e.g., `\"packer_version\": \"...\"`) so the repair pass can skip archives already produced by the current packer. After one repair run per archive, future runs are O(0).\n   - **Tighten the gate** so it only fires on first encounter with a pre-existing archive that lacks the marker.\n\n2. **Fresh-run hot path is `compact_transcript` + `pack_full_generation`** (~70% combined). Worth a closer look but lower priority — at ~9min for 4k checkpoints it's tolerable.\n\nWhich do you want to tackle? My vote is the rerun fix — bigger ROI, smaller blast radius."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3691,"cache_read_input_tokens":166310,"output_tokens":3385,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3691,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":3385,"cache_read_input_tokens":166310,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3691,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3691},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaohjsuAXMpNSdvzcW8mm","type":"assistant","uuid":"119ae612-e017-42a7-86f9-7da008455e98","timestamp":"2026-05-07T18:45:37.406Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"939fabd6-10fa-4faa-9bd3-ce01733dd4f7","version":"2.1.132","gitBranch":"v2-migration-performance"}
